  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Technical Field Manual",
    "overview": "BoxDB uses cool paper, deep ink and cyan to make a developer tool feel direct and inspectable. Working SQL and readable code carry the visual interest; thin rules and generous section spacing keep the surrounding explanation quiet. Preserve the existing cyan B icon and the plain English developer voice.\n\nThe landing page is an invitation to try a client; documentation is a denser reading environment with the same Manrope voice and cyan identity. The built landing display uses Lexend, while Manrope handles supporting headings, body text and documentation. Keep experimental status visible and factual; visual confidence must not imply adoption, performance or production readiness that the project has not established.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool neutral surfaces with cyan reserved for identity, selected states and meaningful emphasis.",
      "Large, compact landing display paired with calm, spacious technical prose.",
      "Real code, ruled ledgers and SVG diagrams instead of decorative imagery.",
      "Native links and controls with visible keyboard focus and narrow-screen reflow."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Cyan Field Rule",
        "body": "Cyan may occupy a whole functional code field as well as small controls; use it to identify something worth inspecting or acting on, not as unrelated decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Code Is Content Rule",
